1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,620
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,970
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,630
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:09,000
I've worked the railroad
for thirty years.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,780
Walking on rail ballast

6
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:14,020
and climbing on and off
rail cars every shift.

7
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:15,050
I had my right knee

8
00:00:15,050 --> 00:00:17,120
replaced two years ago.

9
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:19,440
It has hurt every day
since.

10
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,510
Not surgery pain.

11
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:22,710
I know what that felt
like,

12
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:24,180
and it went away.

13
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,170
This is different.

14
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:25,900
Tight.

15
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:26,740
Full.

16
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,790
Like a band around

17
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:30,310
the joint that never
loosens.

18
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:31,270
And for two years

19
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:33,090
I've been told the same
thing.

20
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:34,250
Give it time.

21
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:35,920
At six weeks it was
swelling,

22
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,480
and swelling is normal.

23
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:38,190
At three months,

24
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:39,350
give it six.

25
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,330
At six months,

26
00:00:40,330 --> 00:00:41,940
some knees take a full
year.

27
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:42,780
At a year,

28
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,930
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

29
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:46,180
And I didn't just wait.

30
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,630
We went down the list.

31
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:49,210
More physical therapy.

32
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:50,020
Every session,

33
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:52,070
every exercise at home.

34
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:53,150
I got stronger.

35
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:54,660
The tightness never moved.

36
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,080
The pain pills helped,

37
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,510
and that was the problem.

38
00:00:57,510 --> 00:00:59,650
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:00,610
and nobody could tell me

40
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:02,180
when I'd get to stop.

41
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,590
Then a nerve block.

42
00:01:03,590 --> 00:01:05,380
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

43
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:06,630
And after that, a second

44
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:07,680
operation to go back

45
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,700
in and do it over.

46
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:09,850
I said no.

47
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:11,920
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

48
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:12,910
and my knee felt like

49
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:14,520
a band was wrapped around
it,

50
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:17,010
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

51
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:18,950
Every morning I took
something for it

52
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:20,220
and went to work.

53
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,610
Couldn't do the stairs,

54
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:22,750
couldn't stand at the
counter

55
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:24,250
long enough to finish
dinner,

56
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,700
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

57
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,890
game without shifting
every two minutes.

58
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:30,500
At work, I couldn't climb
a rail car ladder

59
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,380
without stopping halfway.

60
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:33,350
The guys on my crew

61
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:36,140
started walking the long
end of the yard for me.

62
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:37,500
Nobody said anything.

63
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,720
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,140
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,170
like getting in the car

66
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:42,530
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:43,830
into a decision.

68
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:45,230
After a long and serious

69
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:46,260
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:48,520
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,700
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,470
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:53,070
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:55,590
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:57,680
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,790
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:58,790 --> 00:02:00,110
Only this time there

78
00:02:00,110 --> 00:02:01,670
was no new number.

79
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:02,760
Nobody said

80
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,110
give it another six
months.

81
00:02:04,110 --> 00:02:05,890
There was nothing left to
give it.

82
00:02:05,890 --> 00:02:06,880
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:07,740
lot for a while.

84
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,250
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,140
Then explain this.

86
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:13,240
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

87
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:15,030
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:17,280
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

89
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,150
Everyone in the house was
asleep

90
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:20,850
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

91
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:22,090
with my leg up,

92
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:23,690
trying to find any angle
where

93
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:24,870
it didn't feel like
something

94
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:26,150
was wrapped around my knee

95
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,240
and tightening.

96
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,820
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

97
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,960
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

98
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:33,180
And I just thought,

99
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:35,150
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:36,860
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:38,750
So I made myself a
promise.

102
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:39,650
I wouldn't go a day

103
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,410
without looking for an
answer.

104
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:42,820
And when I found one,

105
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:43,930
I'd share it with everyone

106
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:45,480
going through the same
thing.

107
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,500
So I got my laptop

108
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,750
out and went looking.

109
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,080
Not for a product.

110
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,600
For an explanation.

111
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,160
Mayo Clinic forums,

112
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,360
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

113
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:57,440
doctor videos, medical
animations.

114
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,410
And that's when I found

115
00:02:58,410 --> 00:03:00,120
a video from a physical
therapist

116
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,750
named Dr.

117
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:03,030
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

118
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,950
had been through exactly
this.

119
00:03:04,950 --> 00:03:07,050
But before I say anything
else,

120
00:03:07,050 --> 00:03:08,820
I want to be straight with
you.

121
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,090
You've already had
something work fast.

122
00:03:11,090 --> 00:03:12,090
The ice.

123
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:13,990
The first week of a new
pill.

124
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:15,400
The good day after a
session.

125
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,580
Then it wore off.

126
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,060
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

127
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,020
Fast relief isn't relief.

128
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,320
It's a preview.

129
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,680
So I'm not going to tell

130
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,360
you this works fast.

131
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,400
It doesn't.

132
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,590
But if you're willing to
be patient,

133
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:30,380
and to look at what's

134
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:32,180
going on around your new
knee

135
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:33,850
instead of inside it,
there

136
00:03:33,850 --> 00:03:36,230
is a real reason it still
hurts.

137
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:38,470
And something you can do
about it.

138
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:39,730
Let me explain what he
said,

139
00:03:39,730 --> 00:03:41,040
because this is what
changed

140
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,590
everything for me.

141
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:44,300
He started with the
basics.

142
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,670
A knee replacement takes
out

143
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:47,280
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

144
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,450
in metal and plastic.

145
00:03:48,450 --> 00:03:50,760
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

146
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,560
you had before the
operation.

147
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:54,020
That part I already knew.

148
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,200
But then he explained
something

149
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,590
nobody had ever told me.

150
00:03:56,590 --> 00:03:56,950
He said,

151
00:03:56,950 --> 00:03:58,100
think about a swollen foot

152
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,240
inside a shoe.

153
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,760
The shoe didn't shrink.

154
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,810
Your foot is taking up
more room,

155
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:04,330
so everything feels
cramped

156
00:04:04,330 --> 00:04:06,340
and tight and squeezed.

157
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,360
Your new knee sits

158
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:09,440
in a limited space with
living

159
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:11,450
tissue packed all around
it.

160
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:13,220
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

161
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,990
had to work through that
tissue.

162
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:18,360
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

163
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,030
At first that's normal.

164
00:04:20,030 --> 00:04:22,490
But in some people that
swelling can

165
00:04:22,490 --> 00:04:25,350
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

166
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:27,190
And swollen tissue takes
up more

167
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:29,240
room than calm tissue
does.

168
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,410
So when you bend,

169
00:04:30,410 --> 00:04:32,760
that tissue gets
compressed.

170
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:33,830
When you straighten,

171
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:35,540
it gets pulled tight.

172
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,870
That's the band.

173
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:39,830
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

174
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:40,670
And you start being

175
00:04:40,670 --> 00:04:41,340
the one who says,

176
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:42,140
you go ahead.

177
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:43,620
I'll stay here.

178
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,170
And that's exactly why so
much

179
00:04:45,170 --> 00:04:46,920
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

180
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,940
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

181
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:50,120
around the knee.

182
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,160
Worth doing,

183
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,210
and I'd done it.

184
00:04:52,210 --> 00:04:53,650
It does nothing about
tissue

185
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:54,820
taking up room.

186
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,070
A nerve block quiets

187
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:58,050
the nerve carrying the
signal.

188
00:04:58,050 --> 00:05:00,640
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

189
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,200
But when that irritated
tissue

190
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,760
finally calms down,

191
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,230
it holds less fluid,

192
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:07,170
and it takes up less room.

193
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:08,540
Less room taken up means

194
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,730
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

195
00:05:10,730 --> 00:05:12,770
That's what takes the
pressure off.

196
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,260
After two years of this,

197
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,190
it finally made sense.

198
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,250
The problem was never the
new knee.

199
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,500
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

200
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:22,120
He calls it the squeeze.

201
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:24,840
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

202
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:28,150
I'd bought knee sleeves,
knee pads for work,

203
00:05:28,150 --> 00:05:30,790
compression braces,
creams,

204
00:05:30,790 --> 00:05:32,430
half of Amazon really,

205
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:34,930
and all any of it gave me
was an hour.

206
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:35,860
I even looked at going

207
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:37,910
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

208
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:39,850
But at $200 a session

209
00:05:39,850 --> 00:05:41,900
with nothing covered by
insurance,

210
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:43,610
that was a quick no.

211
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:45,160
Then one night
after a shift

212
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,230
I went back to that knee
replacement group

213
00:05:47,230 --> 00:05:48,640
and actually read it.

214
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,220
Thousands of people,

215
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:51,910
years out from surgery,

216
00:05:51,910 --> 00:05:54,290
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

217
00:05:54,290 --> 00:05:56,000
nobody could explain.

218
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,770
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

219
00:05:57,770 --> 00:05:59,860
the same thing kept coming
up.

220
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,500
This one device,

221
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,570
and people saying it was
the first

222
00:06:03,570 --> 00:06:05,280
thing that made a
difference.

223
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,030
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

224
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:08,730
alright, here it comes,

225
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:10,290
he's selling me something,

226
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:12,450
let me shut that down
right now.

227
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:14,180
I'm only here because I
made myself

228
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,070
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

229
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:17,090
that if I ever found

230
00:06:17,090 --> 00:06:18,220
something that helped,

231
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:19,620
I'd say so.

232
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,250
It's called the KenRelief
Red

233
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:22,930
Light Therapy Wrap.

234
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:25,310
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

235
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:26,360
It looked like the cheap

236
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,680
knee sleeves off Amazon

237
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,140
that did nothing for me.

238
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,160
But I went to their
website anyway,

239
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,030
just to see what all

240
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:33,470
the fuss was about.

241
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:35,390
It's the same red light
therapy

242
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:38,480
clinics charge $200 a
session

243
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,890
for, off machines that
cost

244
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,480
fifty thousand dollars,

245
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,480
in a wrap you plug

246
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,180
into the wall at home.

247
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,900
Two hundred and forty
lights.

248
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:48,230
Red at 660 nanometers

249
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:50,750
and near-infrared at 850,

250
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,190
run together for the
strongest effect.

251
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:54,620
Four strength levels.

252
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,470
A five to thirty minute
timer.

253
00:06:56,470 --> 00:06:58,060
Then I saw the guarantee.

254
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,410
Ninety days.

255
00:06:59,410 --> 00:07:01,280
Results or your money
back,

256
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,870
no questions, no store
credit,

257
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:05,910
and you don't even send it
back.

258
00:07:05,910 --> 00:07:08,130
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

259
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:09,580
days to change my mind.

260
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:11,270
There wasn't much to lose,

261
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:12,740
so I ordered it.

262
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,340
Two of them, actually.

263
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,520
Only the right knee was
replaced,

264
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,720
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

265
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,770
and I'd done it for two
years.

266
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:23,130
The left one was carrying
the difference.

267
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:23,850
When it came,

268
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:26,120
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

269
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,430
because I'd been let down
too

270
00:07:27,430 --> 00:07:29,390
many times to get excited.

271
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:31,180
What I felt was warmth.

272
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,490
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

273
00:07:33,490 --> 00:07:35,170
More like it was coming
from inside

274
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:36,690
the knee and spreading
around it.

275
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:37,680
And that was it.

276
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,230
That was the whole
experience.

277
00:07:39,230 --> 00:07:40,490
When I took it off,

278
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:41,100
I'll be honest,

279
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:43,080
nothing dramatic had
happened.

280
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,570
And after what that video
said,

281
00:07:44,570 --> 00:07:46,460
that's exactly what I
expected.

282
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:47,630
What was different

283
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:48,620
was that for the first

284
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:49,980
time in two years

285
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:51,750
I'd done something for my
knee

286
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:53,230
instead of to it.

287
00:07:53,230 --> 00:07:54,220
Twenty minutes,

288
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:56,650
in my own chair,
after my shift.

289
00:07:56,650 --> 00:07:58,760
No drive, no copay.

290
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,580
They say twenty minutes.

291
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,510
I did thirty,

292
00:08:01,510 --> 00:08:02,600
twice a day,

293
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,660
lowest setting that first
week.

294
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:07,370
I put it on the calendar,
around my shifts.

295
00:08:07,370 --> 00:08:08,100
The first week,

296
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:08,880
I couldn't have told

297
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,360
you if anything was
happening.

298
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,170
I tried not to get

299
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,270
my hopes up.

300
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:13,980
I'd had things help for a
week

301
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:15,210
and then stop.

302
00:08:15,210 --> 00:08:16,590
But somewhere in the
second week

303
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:17,750
I noticed I'd come down

304
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,750
the stairs without holding
the rail.

305
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,030
I hadn't decided to.

306
00:08:21,030 --> 00:08:22,200
I just did it,

307
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,480
then stopped halfway down

308
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,840
because I realized.

309
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,120
By the end of the fourth
week

310
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,260
I'd slept through the
night

311
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:29,220
four times running.

312
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:30,170
I stood at the counter

313
00:08:30,170 --> 00:08:31,210
and finished making dinner

314
00:08:31,210 --> 00:08:33,120
without looking for the
stool.

315
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:34,760
None of that is dramatic.

316
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,660
All of it was gone

317
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,920
for two years.

318
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:38,470
A few weeks later my wife
asked

319
00:08:38,470 --> 00:08:39,360
if I wanted to walk

320
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,320
the long way around the
block.

321
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,170
And for the first time

322
00:08:42,170 --> 00:08:42,920
in two years,

323
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,190
I said yes.

324
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:45,710
I wanted to understand
why,

325
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:47,240
so I read the whole thing.

326
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:49,000
It comes down to four
steps.

327
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:49,790
One.

328
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:51,710
The tissue around a new
knee can

329
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:55,060
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

330
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:56,140
Two.

331
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:58,100
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

332
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,080
so it takes up more

333
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,550
room than it should.

334
00:09:00,550 --> 00:09:01,410
Three.

335
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:03,210
There's only so much room
in there.

336
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:04,930
Bending compresses it.

337
00:09:04,930 --> 00:09:06,700
Straightening pulls it
tight.

338
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:08,140
That's the squeeze.

339
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:08,860
Four.

340
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:10,910
Red and near-infrared
light have been

341
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:13,280
studied for calming that
inflammation,

342
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,600
so the swelling and the
pressure

343
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,010
can come down with it.

344
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:17,700
In a randomized trial,

345
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,620
patients given light
therapy after

346
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:20,780
a knee replacement

347
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:22,170
had less pain,

348
00:09:22,170 --> 00:09:23,160
less swelling

349
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,790
and better early movement
than

350
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:25,910
those who weren't.

351
00:09:25,910 --> 00:09:28,490
A 2025 review said the
same,

352
00:09:28,490 --> 00:09:29,680
and was clear the evidence

353
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,960
is still limited.

354
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,890
I probably sound like
a broken record

355
00:09:32,890 --> 00:09:34,720
to the guys on my crew.

356
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,590
But after two years of
doing everything

357
00:09:36,590 --> 00:09:38,880
I was told and getting
nowhere,

358
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,390
you have no idea what it's

359
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:42,050
like to sleep through the
night,

360
00:09:42,050 --> 00:09:43,530
say yes to the walk,

361
00:09:43,530 --> 00:09:45,130
and get my life back.

362
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:46,900
So take it from me.

363
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,900
Don't spend another year
waiting

364
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:49,910
for it to settle.

365
00:09:49,910 --> 00:09:52,010
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

366
00:09:52,010 --> 00:09:53,370
More than ten thousand
people

367
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:54,520
with pain after a knee

368
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,500
replacement have already
tried this.

369
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:58,490
Some had it worse than I
did.

370
00:09:58,490 --> 00:09:59,640
You can get the KenRelief

371
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,210
wrap from their website,

372
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:02,660
with a discount link

373
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:04,370
and ninety days to try it.

374
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:06,130
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

375
00:10:06,130 --> 00:10:07,370
you get your money back

376
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:08,870
and you keep the wrap.

377
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:10,610
They only release so many

378
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,970
at that price.

379
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:13,500
If it's still there,

380
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:14,190
get one,

381
00:10:14,190 --> 00:10:16,000
and stop the squeeze.

